SEC-FILES-001.remediation:
Remove or restrict access to sensitive files:

For Apache (.htaccess):
<FilesMatch "\.(git|env|sql|zip|tar\.gz)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

For Nginx:
location ~ /\.git {
    deny all;
}
location ~ /\. {
    deny all;
}
location ~ \.(sql|zip|tar\.gz)$ {
    deny all;
}

Best practices:
1. Don't deploy .git directories to production
2. Use .gitignore for sensitive files
3. Store config outside webroot
4. Disable directory listing

