SEC-CACHE-001.remediation:
Add Cache-Control headers to prevent caching on sensitive paths:

Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
Pragma: no-cache
Expires: 0

For Apache (.htaccess in sensitive directories):
<FilesMatch "\.(html|htm|php)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private"
    Header set Pragma "no-cache"
    Header set Expires "0"
</FilesMatch>

For Nginx:
location ~ ^/(login|account|admin) {
    add_header Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private" always;
    add_header Pragma "no-cache" always;
    add_header Expires "0" always;
}

For Express/Node.js:
app.use('/login', (req, res, next) => {
  res.set({
    'Cache-Control': 'no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private',
    'Pragma': 'no-cache',
    'Expires': '0'
  });
  next();
});

